KNOWNBUG libstdcxx16
main.cpp
--cpp26
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ embedded bytes: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
A probe of the C++26 support census (2026-11-05): #embed ([cpp.embed]) of a
3-byte file: the preprocessor produces the bytes as a comma-separated list, so
CBMC sees an ordinary initializer. Needs a preprocessor implementing #embed
(GCC 15 or later; tagged libstdcxx16 as that tag checks the host gcc's
version)..  The last assertion is WRONG and must fail, so a pass is not
vacuous.
